{{fbdoc item="title" value="Graphics file and text drops"}}----
Receive bounded native drag-and-drop payloads through gfxlib2 or gfxlib3.

{{fbdoc item="desc"}}
	Include ##fbdrop.bi## and call ##FBC.screenDropEnable## after opening a graphics mode. Pass nonzero to enable reception; pass zero to disable it. The function returns ##FB.DROP_OK## when enabled, or ##FB.DROP_UNAVAILABLE## when the current driver has no drop support. Disabling drops or changing graphics modes discards retained payloads.

	The available native adapters accept Windows shell file drops and X11 local-file or UTF-8 text drops. Other drivers report that the service is unavailable. A file drop returns local path text; the runtime does not open paths, fetch remote locations, or execute dropped text.

{{fbdoc item="section" value="ScreenEvent payload"}}
	When ##[[KeyPgScreenevent|ScreenEvent]]## returns an ##FB.EVENT_DROP## event, its ##.drop_id## is the payload identifier, ##.drop_count## is the number of items, and ##.drop_kind## is ##FB.DROP_FILES## or ##FB.DROP_TEXT##. Copy each item with ##FBC.screenDropGet## before the retained payload expires:

%%(freebasic)
#include once "fbdrop.bi"
Using FB
Using FBC

Dim event As EVENT
If ScreenEvent(@event) Then
	If event.type = EVENT_DROP Then
		Dim item As Long
		For item = 0 To event.drop_count - 1
			Dim payload As String
			If screenDropGet(event.drop_id, item, payload) = DROP_OK Then
				Print payload
			End If
		Next item
	End If
End If
%%

{{fbdoc item="section" value="Limits and lifetime"}}
	A drop contains at most ##FB.DROP_MAX_ITEMS## (64) items and ##FB.DROP_MAX_BYTES## (65,536) bytes including terminators. The runtime retains at most ##FB.DROP_RETAINED## (8) recent payloads for the current mode. A payload can expire as later drops arrive; copy items promptly into application-owned strings.

	##FBC.screenDropGet## returns an owned UTF-8 ##[[KeyPgString|String]]##. It returns ##FB.DROP_INVALID## for an invalid identifier or item index, ##FB.DROP_FAILED## if copying cannot allocate storage, and ##FB.DROP_EXPIRED## if the payload is no longer retained. The result string is independent of the native event memory and remains owned by the caller.

